### The mark-sweep case changed, on purpose

`churn_mark_sweep` used to say "no promotion, so the elder budget holds the blocks; peak 36 MB,
`major=42`, `by_elder_exhausted=42`". In mark-sweep every array is born in the elder space, so with
the takeover path its block is registered as soon as the array gets it. That is the correct reading
of "a block held by an elder value must count", but it changes which budget drives the collections.
After the fix the same case reports:

```
gc_block_churn base=0 peak=7200000 low=2400000 ... total=180000000
[camel] gc: major=300 requested=300 ... by_elder_block_budget=300 ... by_elder_exhausted=0 minor=0 ...
        elder_block_live_mb=2.3 elder_block_budget_mb=4.0
```

The peak falls from 36 MB to 7.2 MB (one 2.4 MB temporary plus the 4 MB floor) and the cause moves
from the elder-space budget to the promoted-block budget. The test's description and assertions were
updated to the new behavior; keeping the old ones would assert that a born-elder block is invisible,
which is exactly the defect this task fixes. This is the only existing expectation the change
necessitated.

